`cuda_graph_dynamic_microbatches `is required exactly when scheduler + TE graphs + PP > 1;
Functionally, it only enables a check on the microbatch idx. So it adds no real new behavior that cant already be inferred from existing configs.
Could we just drop it, and replace the configs this knob rejects with a derived condition for scheduler + TE graphs + PP > 1? Can we also just default to the stronger check in module.py
